From: cheng343 <203324649+cheng343@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:24:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] plugins: fetch the store through the GitHub contents API
 first

Recovery cannot reach raw.githubusercontent.com on filtered networks, and in
that case the store page fails with "Could not download the AERA plugin
catalog." The contents API lives on api.github.com, the same host the root
manager already updates through on the device.

Every raw.githubusercontent.com file is now also offered as
api.github.com/repos/<owner>/<repo>/contents/<path>?ref=<ref> (base64 inside a
JSON envelope, decoded locally) and tried before the jsDelivr mirror and the
direct URL. The catalog and its signature are fetched with the same decoder,
still from a single source each. All verification stays after the transfer -
Ed25519 signature over the catalog, SHA-256 over every plugin file and the size
limits - so no source can inject data.
